{
    "pageid": 1474,
    "title": "Sons of Abraham",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Sons of Abraham (SoA) is the fifth major expansion for Crusader Kings II , released on November 18, 2013, alongside patch 2.0 ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "It gives further depth to the three Abrahamic faiths; Christianity in particular, but has also added some content for Muslims ; Jewish non-nomadic rulers become playable."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Main features",
            "level": 2,
            "content": []
        },
        {
            "heading": "Papal mechanics",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "College of Cardinals to elect the Pope",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Pope that you supported can give you money, free invasions/excommunications/divorces",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "You can request Crusades !",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Opinion maluses for each request to Pope",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Exclusive to Catholics and Fraticelli",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Holy orders",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Two new Catholic orders (Calatrava and Santiago)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Everybody gets holy order (Immortals confirmed for Zoroastrians)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Characters from court will join (like Varangians)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "You can borrow from them (like historical Templars were bankers)",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Events",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "300+ new ones",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Some are patch, some are DLC",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Patch: events that start Crusades/Jihads/etc",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Flavor events for Abrahamic faiths",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Misc",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Pilgrimages to holy places for Catholics",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Play as a Jewish lord and restore the kingdom of Israel",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Pick sides in Islam as a rationalist Mutazilite or an opposing Ashari",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Retire troublesome courtiers to a monastery as monk or nun",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Heresies can take over as the new orthodoxy if there are 5 more provinces following the heresy than there are that follow the parent religion [1]",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
